The OpenCL kernels in int2_fp16_upcvt/ and int2_via_int2_x_int8_dpas/ are
ports of Intel XeTLA kernels (int2_fp16_upcvt_xmx_xe.hpp,
int2_fp16_dpas_xmx_xe.hpp, int2_bf16_dpas_xmx_xe.hpp) and follow their data
layouts, dequantization and quantization schemes.

The xetla_ref/ and xetla_ref_bf16/ harnesses are derived from the XeTLA test
drivers (int2_fp16_upcvt_dpas_fast_test, int2_fp16_dpas_fp16scales_fast_test,
int2_bf16_dpas_fast_test) and are licensed under the Apache License 2.0; see
LICENSE.xetla.

tools/xetla_epilogue_parity/ compiles against the vLLM xetla plugin's
csrc/int2_fp16_upcvt_kernel.sycl (not redistributed here).

bitcos_fp16_upcvt/ ports the XeTLA BITCOS kernel (bitcos_fp16_upcvt_xmx_xe.hpp)
and follows its layout and unpack sequence. It is benchmarked against the XeTLA
harness bitcos_fp16_dpas_fp16scales_fast_test (not redistributed here).
